<div>
  <h1>JSON API</h1>
</div>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 px-2 pb-8">
  <p class="text-on-surface-variant">
    Interactive documentation for the JSON API. All endpoints accept and return
    <code>application/json</code>. Expand a path to see examples and schema. Any
    request formats will self describe errors in types or missing fields.
  </p>

  <section class="mx-auto prose rounded-md bg-surface-container p-3">
    <h2>Calling the API</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>BEARER_TOKEN</code> in your shell, then include it in the
      <code>Authorization</code> header. The configured token is shown below for
      convenience. Hover over it or focus it with the keyboard to reveal it.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <button
        id="api-bearer-token"
        class="cursor-default rounded bg-surface-container-highest px-2 py-1 font-mono blur-sm transition hover:blur-none focus:blur-none"
        title="Hover or focus to reveal the bearer token"
        type="button"
      >
        {{ bearer_token | e }}
      </button>
      <button
        class="btn-tonal"
        type="button"
        onclick="apiDocs.copyBearerToken(event)"
      >
        <icon>content_copy</icon>
        Copy token
      </button>
      <span id="api-bearer-token-copy-status"></span>
    </div>
    <pre
      class="snippet-example rounded-md bg-surface-container-highest p-1 font-mono"
    >
export BEARER_TOKEN='your-token-here'
curl \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${BEARER_TOKEN}" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "X-Indent: 2" \
  {{ url_for("items.json_all", _external=True) }}</pre>
    <p class="text-on-surface-variant">
      The <code>X-Indent: 2</code> header is optional and formats JSON responses
      with indentation. Remove it for compact responses.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto prose rounded-md bg-surface-container p-3">
    <h2>Client errors</h2>
    <p>
      All <code>4xx</code> responses use the same JSON structure shown below. An
      endpoint with no inputs (no URL, query, or body inputs) will never return
      a <code>4xx</code> response. An endpoint with URL, query, or body inputs
      may return a <code>4xx</code> response when those inputs are invalid or
      missing.
    </p>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-1 py-1">
      <button
        class="btn-example btn-tonal"
        onclick="apiDocs.loadSnippet(event)"
      >
        Example
      </button>
      <button class="btn-schema btn-text" onclick="apiDocs.loadSnippet(event)">
        Schema
      </button>
    </div>
    <pre
      class="snippet-example rounded-md bg-surface-container-highest p-1 font-mono"
    >
{{- error_response.example_json | e -}}</pre>
    <pre
      class="snippet-schema hidden rounded-md bg-surface-container-highest p-1 font-mono"
    >
{{- error_response.schema_json | e -}}</pre>
  </section>

  {% for group in groups %}
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-primary">{{ group.name }}</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        {% for p in group.description %}<p>{{ p }}</p>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        {% for op in group.operations %}
          {% include "api/operation.jinja" %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
